      "lineNbr": 959,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-03-14T07:46:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes. That\u0027s the purpose of the API. The native network needs to be destroyed because otherwise the transport will not be able to re-use the same interface to replace the network with a new network. (netd will refuse to put the same interface into two different networks at the same time.)",
      "parentUuid": "bb9bb245_e90dd52e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 958,
        "startChar": 93,
        "endLine": 959,
        "endChar": 29
      },
      "revId": "953ce0fccf0613787b87a4792b067a071e11552e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bda6d797_3c7b3d34",
        "filename": "framework/src/android/net/NetworkAgent.java",
        "patchSetId": 27
      },
      "lineNbr": 967,
      "author": {
        "id": 1306837
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-03-10T11:26:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "From above, the native network will be destroyed immediately.\nDoes this mean the network stays CONNECTED but cannot actually be used?\nIf so, is it better to change status to something like DISCONNECTED or SUSPENDED?\nGiven that it will take efforts to clarify issues where the network is CONNECTED but cannot be used. Also some apps might actually rely on the status to do socket stuff.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 967,
        "startChar": 35,
        "endLine": 967,
        "endChar": 44
      },
      "revId": "953ce0fccf0613787b87a4792b067a071e11552e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0a618a0d_a875b965",
        "filename": "framework/src/android/net/NetworkAgent.java",
        "patchSetId": 27
      },
      "lineNbr": 967,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-03-14T07:46:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, that\u0027s what it means. This is working as designed: the network is in a \"frozen\" state where nothing that affects scoring can change. The primary use case is to prevent the device from switching to cell data while wifi is roaming from one network to another.\n\nNo callbacks are sent because network scoring is tightly coupled to NetworkCallbacks. Sending callbacks in this case would require adding a fair bit of complexity. (Simple example: because the network must remain the default network, getActiveNetwork must continue to return it. So onLost doesn\u0027t really make much sense. But if we don\u0027t send onLost, and we mark the network disconnected, then the network became disconnected without sending onLost, which is wrong.) For similar reasons, the network is not marked disconnected. It\u0027s as if it was \"frozen\": nothing changes.\n\nMarking it as suspended would be possible I think. That might be helpful to apps, but on the other hand, this API should not affect scoring. If we do this, it means that we will not be able to use NOT_SUSPENDED to affect scoring. Not sure if we want to do that. For now, left as is.",
      "parentUuid": "bda6d797_3c7b3d34",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 967,
        "startChar": 35,
        "endLine": 967,
        "endChar": 44
      },
      "revId": "953ce0fccf0613787b87a4792b067a071e11552e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "66a7841e_b01d66e0",
        "filename": "framework/src/android/net/NetworkAgent.java",
        "patchSetId": 27
      },
      "lineNbr": 967,
      "author": {
        "id": 1306837
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-03-14T09:50:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It seems to me to affect scoring should not be a reason of preventing us from using the correct capabilities.\nMayhaps in long term we could use tricks like how we manage unvalidated networks.\nBut agree to left it as is.",
      "parentUuid": "0a618a0d_a875b965",
      "range": {
